# Where the Go API lives.
#
# Leave this unset for the normal deployment. The site and the API run as two services in one
# Vercel project behind one domain, so `/api/options` is same-origin — a relative URL is both the
# correct one and the one that never has to think about CORS.
#
# Set it only when the two are split across origins: a local Go server while developing, or an API
# on its own box. Then the API's ALLOWED_ORIGINS has to name this site in turn.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://api.example.com
